<title>BELGIUM: EU moving to open talks with six countries.</title>
<headline>EU moving to open talks with six countries.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission plans to recommend opening membership talks with five eastern European countries and Cyprus next week, EU officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The assessment that the (EU Commission) services have made to date would suggest that they would recommend on the basis of objective criteria to start negotiations with six,&quot; one official, who declined to be named, told Reuters.  </p>
<p>Another official told Reuters that Poland, Hungary and the Czech Republic, the widely acknowledged frontrunners, were expected to be recommended when the EU executive presents its assessments of how ready each of 10 eastern European hopefuls are for the rigours of EU membership on July 16.</p>
<p>A preliminary document prepared by the executive and under scrutiny by the 20 Commissioners also signals that Estonia and Slovenia are ready for membership, he said.</p>
<p>Latvia, Lithuania, Bulgaria, Romania and Slovakia have also applied for EU membership.</p>
</text>
